{"id":"da283e79-cf72-43a6-b451-40c1560dc1a1","object":"chat.completion","created":1785019852,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {}\\n    rank = {}\\n    def make_set(x):\\n        parent[x] = x\\n        rank[x] = 0\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    for v in nodes:\\n        make_set(v)\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        mr = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n    edges.sort()\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for mr, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr])\\n            total_weight += mr\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Disconnected input\\\")\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate a Python implementation for solve(case) that computes mutual-reachability MST given nodes, core_distance dict, and distances list. The function must return a dict with \"mst_edges\" (list of [node1, node2, weight] where node1<node2? The output schema expects prefixItems: [string, string, number] and minItems=3 maxItems=3. So each edge is [string, string, number]. The specification says \"Canonicalize undirected endpoints.\" So we should sort the node names lexicographically? Probably yes to ensure deterministic order. Also note: \"Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs.\" For Kruskal, we need to sort edges by weight (mutual reachability) and then tie-break by endpoint IDs. Then run union-find.\n\nInput: case has fields \"nodes\", \"core_distance\", \"distances\". \"nodes\" is list of node IDs (strings). \"core_distance\" is dict mapping node to core distance (number). \"distances\" is list of [node1, node2, distance] (all nodes present, presumably complete graph? But we only need edges from distances list? Actually distances provide all pairwise distances? The list may be complete undirected graph? Not necessarily but it should contain all pairs. Compute mutual reachability for each pair: max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then build list of edges (node_i, node_j, mr). We need to add only those? The distances list contains each pair once? It's undirected. So we have all pairs. Then sort edges by mr, then node1, node2 (after canonicalization). Then Kruskal.\n\nMust also check for disconnected inputs? The problem says \"Reject disconnected inputs\". If the graph is disconnected after considering all edges? Actually mutual reachability graph is complete because distances are provided for all pairs? It should be complete because distances list includes all pairs. But core distances might be missing? No, core_distance has all nodes. So graph is complete. But if there are fewer than n-1 edges? No, it's complete. So disconnected not possible. But we can still check: after MST, number of edges should be len(nodes)-1, else raise? The spec says reject disconnected inputs. Possibly if nodes list has duplicates or empty? We can just compute and if fewer edges, raise error. But we must ensure we only add edges from distances list (which is complete). So MST will be connected. So we can skip explicit disconnect check but it's safe.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case): extract nodes, core_dist, distances. Create union-find class. Build edges list: for each (u, v, d) in distances, canonicalize (sorted), mr = max(core_dist[u], core_dist[v], d). Append (mr, u, v). Sort edges by (mr, u, v). Initialize UF. mst_edges = [], total_weight=0. For each (mr, u, v) in sorted edges: if UF.find(u) != UF.find(v): UF.union(u,v); mst_edges.append([u, v, mr]); total_weight += mr; if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes)-1: break. After loop, if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes)-1: raise ValueError(\"disconnected\"). Return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}.\n\nNote: sorting endpoints: we sorted u,v by string comparison. Also edges in mst_edges should have canonical ordering as produced. The output schema doesn't require sorted output order, but we output as we added.\n\nAlso ensure no mutation of case.\n\nNow produce the implementation string. Must be valid JSON string. Code must be Python source.\n\nWe'll output the JSON with single key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as escaped string.\n\nI'll write the code.\n\nPotential issues: Core distance may be float; distances may be float. Union-find implementation with path compression.\n\nAlso note: \"Canonicalize undirected endpoints.\" means we should order the two nodes in a consistent way. Usually alphabetical. We'll do that.\n\nEdge sorting: \"Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs.\" So after sorting by mr, then by node1, then node2. Since we already sorted node order when creating.\n\nNow produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1937,"completion_tokens":1348,"total_tokens":3285,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":914},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":17},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}